From: MatonOS audio team
Subject: [PATCH] spa: build ALSA plugin for Android Linux kernels

The NDK cross file reports the target OS as Android, although MatonOS runs
on the Linux kernel and uses ALSA/libudev for hardware discovery. Include
Android in the ALSA SPA plugin condition so WirePlumber can enumerate cards.

--- a/spa/plugins/meson.build
+++ b/spa/plugins/meson.build
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
-if alsa_dep.found() and host_machine.system() == 'linux'
+# Android userspace still uses the Linux ALSA kernel interface. Meson reports
+# the NDK target as "android", so include it when building the ALSA SPA plugin.
+if alsa_dep.found() and host_machine.system() in ['linux', 'android']
   subdir('alsa')
 endif
*** End Patch
